--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/db/migrations/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+# Migrations
+
+Baseline (R-DB-02, 2026-09-25):
+
+- `0000`: generated from `src/db/schemas`.
+- `0001`: custom, `CREATE EXTENSION postgis` (search's `ST_Distance`).
+- `0002`: custom, idempotent: `btree_gist` plus the `rental_requests_no_overlap`
+  exclusion constraint, and the `system` user row. drizzle-kit can't express
+  either, so they live only here. Integration tests run this file by hand
+  against `db:push`-built databases.
+
+Future migrations start at `0003`. Generate them with `bun run db:generate`;
+use `--custom` only for what drizzle can't express (a custom migration
+doesn't update the snapshot).
+
+**`db:migrate` runs every pending migration in one transaction.** So a
+migration can't use an enum value added by another migration in the same
+run, and `CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY` can't go through `db:migrate` at all.
+
+**A fresh environment isn't fully bootstrapped by `db:migrate` alone.** After
+migrating, run these in order (each is idempotent):
+
+    bun run seed:listing-categories
+    bun run seed:service-categories
+    bun run seed:communities-real   # KC Metro only, no test fixtures
+
+`bun run seed` (full) truncates every table and loads fake users, rentals,
+payments and messages. Dev and e2e only; never run it against a real
+environment.
+
+Environments that existed before the baseline (dev, staging) were marked as
+having `0000`–`0002` applied with one `drizzle.__drizzle_migrations` row
+instead of running them (see R-DB-02 Step 5). Never run `db:migrate` on such
+an environment before that row exists.
+
+History before the baseline is archived in
+`src/db/migrations-archive-pre-0000/` for reference; nothing reads it.
